  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.0-preview2\n- Adds TestRunReportFormatter for canonical plain-text report rendering.\n- Consumers can now call TestRunReportFormatter.Format(report) to produce\n  human-readable output for console, CI logs, bug reports, or any text sink.\n\nv1.0.0-preview1\n- First v1 preview release of Circuids.Pulse.\n- Locks the one-package in-app runner model for real host conformance tests.\n- Marks Pulse ready for real project adoption and production conformance pilots while stable v1 feedback is gathered from the .NET community.\n- Reinforces Pulse conformance tests as an extra runtime verification layer, not a replacement for unit, integration, UI, end-to-end, or other existing test types.\n- Adds v1 report schema metadata and total run duration to TestRunReport.\n- Enforces one active Pulse run per host service provider.\n- Skips suite tests after InitializeAsync failure while still running teardown.\n- Documents the canonical TestSupport / Tests / ConformanceHost structure.\n\nv0.1.1-Experimental\n- Minor fixes for build pipeline.\n\nv0.1.0-Experimental\n- Initial release of Circuids.Pulse",
